  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 712.11 Monitoring Frequency for SOC Contaminants",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 712.11 Monitoring Frequency for SOC Contaminants.\n\n(a) The O/O of a community water system or non-transient, non-community water system shall monitor for SOCs on an annual basis, except that monitoring shall not be required for aldicarb, aldicarb sulfoxide, or aldicarb sulfone.\n\n(b) The O/O of a community water system or non-transient non-community water system at which no SOC listed in Env-Dw 705.02 is detected may apply to the department for a waiver from the requirement of this section as specified in Env-Dw 712.21.\n\n(c) The department shall reduce the sampling frequency to a minimum of one sample every 3 years or every 6 years if a waiver is granted pursuant to Env-Dw 712.21.\n\nSource. #9700, eff 5-1-10; ss by #12668, eff 1-1-19 (formerly Env-Dw 712.10)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw700.html"
